## Context

Celebrate sweep after raid 419-420 (PR #712): the 0419 class — duplicated
reference-path default constants — has a GEM twin that 0419's scope
(vietnam_thermal_v1.csv only) did not cover:

- `src/aedist/tabulate_reconciliation.py:36` `_GEM_REF` (gem_thermal.csv)
- `scripts/audit_source_urls.py:39` `_DEFAULT_GEM` (gem_thermal.csv)
- make-side `render.mk:83 ANALYSIS_GEM_REF` is the single point — fine.

The 0419 ratchet test (`tests/test_no_hardcoded_reference_path.py`) only
guards the literal `vietnam_thermal_v1.csv`; the CLASS is "any
data/reference CSV filename hardcoded outside config.py".

## Quoi faire

1. Add `DEFAULT_GEM_REFERENCE` to `src/aedist/config.py`; re-point the two
   constants (ruff trap: import + usage in one edit batch).
2. Generalize the ratchet: assert NO `*.csv` filename under `data/reference/`
   appears in string literals in `src/aedist/*.py` outside config.py
   (docstrings/comments exempt, same AST mechanics as the existing test).
3. Consider scripts/ coverage in the ratchet (0419 fixed scripts/ consumers
   but the test does not guard them).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Zero gem_thermal.csv / gem_units.csv literals in src/ outside config.py
- [ ] Ratchet test covers the class (all data/reference CSV names), not the
      single filename
- [ ] `make check` vert

